  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/iframe-embed-object.html#the-iframe-element:delay-the-load-event says:\r\n\r\n> When the iframe's browsing context's active document is not ready for post-load tasks, and when anything in the iframe is delaying the load event of the iframe's browsing context's active document, and when the iframe's browsing context is in the delaying load events mode, the iframe must delay the load event of its document.\r\n\r\nIs this trying to say that the iframe delays the load event of its document only if all three of these conditions:\r\n\r\n1. iframe's browsing context's active document is not ready for post-load tasks\r\n2. anything in the iframe is delaying the load event of the iframe's browsing context's active document\r\n3. the iframe's browsing context is in the delaying load events mode\r\n\r\nhold?  Or is it saying that it does so if any of the three holds?\r\n\r\nI _think_ it means \"if any of these holds\", because otherwise load could fire on the parent before firing on the subframe, since condition 3 stops holding during navigation as soon as the new Document is created.  But if the intent is that it's \"if any of these holds\", then the right conjunction is probably \"or\", not \"and\", right?\r\n\r\nSimilar for https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/obsolete.html#frames:delaying-load-events-mode and https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/iframe-embed-object.html#the-embed-element:delaying-load-events-mode and https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/iframe-embed-object.html#the-object-element:delaying-load-events-mode",
